  "schema_version": 1,
  "strategy": "Define the exact and rounded product trees by shape-preserving leaf maps, and define the rounded dot product by roundedSum on the rounded product tree. Construct a leafwise perturbation witness for multiplication using Model.round_spec. Apply the supplied rounded-sum theorem to that rounded product tree, then compose the multiplication perturbation with the addition perturbation using IsPerturbation.trans. The composed bound u + gamma(d,u)*(1+u) equals gamma(d,u) + u*(1+gamma(d,u)); gamma_step bounds it by gamma(d+1,u). Reuse the rounded-sum existential tree as the final witness relative to exactProductTree. This accounts for one multiplication and at most d additions per leaf without assumptions beyond the supplied model and smallness condition.",
